  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 1218 AM MDT Fri Oct 16 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nToday an upper-level ridge moves over North-central, Central, and \nSouthwestern Montana. This brings warm temperatures and dry weather \nto the area today. Today temperatures will be well above seasonal \naverages. Today the pressure gradient increases which will bring \nwindy conditons primarily just to the Rocky Mountain Front. On \nSaturday the upper-level ridge remains over North-central, Central, \nand Southwestern Montana. This will bring warm and dry temperatures \nto the area on Saturday. On Saturday the low-level and mid-level \nwinds increase combined with the upper-level ridge flattening. This \nwill bring windy conditions to North-central Montana with the \nstrongest winds along the Rocky Mountain Front and plains west of I-\n15.\n\nOn Sunday there will be zonal flow (west-east) over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. This will bring slightly cooler \ntemperatures with mostly dry weather. On Monday an upper-level ridge \nbriefly builds in over North-central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana. This will allow temperatures to warm up slightly with \nmostly dry weather. On Tuesday the upper-level ridge remains over \nMontana this will keep warm and dry weather for North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana on Tuesday. On Wednesday and \nThursday there will be a series of weak troughs that pass through \nMontana. This will keep warm and mostly dry weather for North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana on Wednesday and \nThursday. -IG\n\n- Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nOn Saturday there is a 40 - 60% chance for wind gusts of 55 mph or \ngreater along the plains west of I-15. On Saturday along the Rocky \nMountain Front there is a 50 - 80% chance for wind gusts of 70 mph \nor greater. Along the higher peaks of the Rocky Mountain Front there \nis greater than a 70% chance for wind gusts of 75 mph or greater. \nAdditionally the NAEFS (North American Ensemble Forecast System) has \na standardized anomaly greater than 3 for 700 mb winds Saturday \nafternoon across the Rocky Mountain Front and plains west of I-15. \nModels continue to show in excess of 60 to 70 kt 700 mb winds over \nthe Rocky Mountain Front and plains west of I-15 Saturday afternoon \nand evening. As a result a High Wind Watch remains in effect for the \nplains west of I-15 and the Rocky Mountain Front from 9AM Saturday \nthrough 12AM Sunday. On Saturday across the rest of North-central \nMontana there is a 30 - 60% chance for wind gusts of 45 mph or \ngreater. For winds across the Hi-Line east of I-15 there is \ncurrently a low chance to reach and/or exceed high wind criteria but \nif the strong 700 mb winds move east faster than models are \ncurrently depicting a High Wind Watch could be needed for the Hi-\nLine east of I-15. -IG",
